(window.FREE_Q = window.FREE_Q || {})["ssc-cgl"] = {"qs": [["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "In a class, Neha is 12th from the top and 28th from the bottom. How many students are there in the class?", ["41", "38", "40", "39"], 3, "Total = (rank from top) + (rank from bottom) − 1 = 12 + 28 − 1 = 39. Adding without subtracting 1 counts Neha twice and gives the wrong answer 40."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "Statements:\nSome pens are books.\nNo book is a bag.\nConclusions:\nI. Some pens are not bags.\nII. Some bags are pens.", ["Only conclusion I follows", "Neither I nor II follows", "Both I and II follow", "Only conclusion II follows"], 0, "The pens that are books cannot be bags because no book is a bag, so 'some pens are not bags' is definite. Nothing tells us whether any bag is a pen, so II is only a possibility."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "What is the value of sin²30° + cos²60° + tan²45°?", ["5/4", "2", "3/2", "1"], 2, "sin 30° = cos 60° = 1/2, so each square is 1/4, and tan 45° = 1. The sum is 1/4 + 1/4 + 1 = 3/2."], ["General Awareness", "The idea of Fundamental Duties in the Indian Constitution was borrowed from the constitution of which country?", ["United States of America", "Ireland", "Canada", "Erstwhile USSR"], 3, "Fundamental Duties (Article 51A) were inspired by the constitution of the former USSR and added by the 42nd Amendment in 1976. Ireland, by contrast, inspired the Directive Principles of State Policy."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "What is the unit digit of 7⁹⁵?", ["7", "1", "3", "9"], 2, "Unit digits of powers of 7 repeat in a cycle of 4: 7, 9, 3, 1. Since 95 leaves remainder 3 when divided by 4, the unit digit equals that of 7³, which is 3."], ["English Comprehension", "Read the passage and answer the question.\nRainwater harvesting is an old practice that has found new relevance in Indian cities. As groundwater levels fall, many housing societies now collect rooftop runoff and channel it into recharge pits instead of letting it flow into drains. The method is inexpensive and needs little maintenance, yet its benefits depend on cleaning the filters regularly before every monsoon.\nWhich word is closest in meaning to 'relevance' as used in the passage?", ["Expense", "Importance", "Difficulty", "Antiquity"], 1, "The passage says an old practice has found new relevance because groundwater is falling, i.e. it has become important or applicable again. 'Antiquity' refers to oldness, the opposite idea."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "A sum of money doubles itself in 8 years at simple interest. What is the rate of interest per annum?", ["15%", "10%", "12.5%", "8%"], 2, "Doubling means interest equals the principal, i.e. 100% in 8 years. Rate = 100/8 = 12.5% per annum, using SI = P × R × T/100 with SI = P."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "Monthly output of a factory (units): January 400, February 500, March 450, April 650. By what percentage did April's output exceed the average output of January to March?", ["30%", "44 4/9%", "62.5%", "40%"], 1, "Average for January–March = (400 + 500 + 450)/3 = 450 units. April exceeded it by 200, and 200/450 × 100 = 44 4/9% (about 44.4%)."], ["English Comprehension", "Choose the word opposite in meaning to the word in capitals.\nMy grandfather led a FRUGAL life even after he became rich.", ["Thrifty", "Extravagant", "Careful", "Modest"], 1, "'Frugal' means careful and sparing with money. Its opposite is 'extravagant', meaning spending too much. 'Thrifty' and 'careful' are synonyms, not antonyms."], ["English Comprehension", "Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.\nHe is senior than me / in the office / by three years / and earns more.", ["and earns more", "in the office", "He is senior than me", "by three years"], 2, "Latin comparatives such as senior, junior, superior and inferior take 'to', not 'than'. The correct form is 'He is senior to me'."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "Find the next pair in the series.\nAZ, BY, CX, ?", ["DW", "EW", "DV", "DX"], 0, "The first letters move forward one step (A, B, C, D) while the second letters move backward one step (Z, Y, X, W). Hence the next pair is DW."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "Statement: P > Q ≥ R = S < T\nConclusions:\nI. P > S\nII. Q > T", ["Only conclusion II follows", "Neither I nor II follows", "Both I and II follow", "Only conclusion I follows"], 3, "P > Q ≥ R = S gives P > S, so I is true. Q and T are both linked to S in opposite directions (Q ≥ S < T), so no definite relation exists between Q and T; II does not follow."], ["General Awareness", "Which type of mirror is used as a rear-view mirror in vehicles?", ["Cylindrical mirror", "Convex mirror", "Concave mirror", "Plane mirror"], 1, "A convex mirror always forms an erect, diminished image and gives a wider field of view, which helps drivers see more traffic behind. Concave mirrors are used in torches and shaving mirrors."], ["English Comprehension", "Which of the following words is spelt correctly?", ["Embarass", "Embarrass", "Emberrass", "Embarras"], 1, "The correct spelling is 'embarrass', with double 'r' and double 's'. The other options drop one of the doubled letters or change the vowel."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "The circumference of a circle is 88 cm. What is its area? (Take π = 22/7)", ["1232 cm²", "154 cm²", "308 cm²", "616 cm²"], 3, "2πr = 88 gives r = 88 × 7/44 = 14 cm. Area = πr² = 22/7 × 14 × 14 = 616 cm². 154 cm² is the area for radius 7 cm."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "Find the next term of the series.\n2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?", ["44", "36", "42", "40"], 2, "The terms are 1×2, 2×3, 3×4, 4×5 and 5×6, so the next term is 6×7 = 42. Equivalently the differences 4, 6, 8, 10 increase by 2, giving 30 + 12."], ["English Comprehension", "Select the most appropriate meaning of the idiom 'to burn the midnight oil'.", ["To work or study late into the night", "To waste money on useless things", "To lose one's temper suddenly", "To destroy evidence of a mistake"], 0, "'To burn the midnight oil' refers to staying up late to work or study, originally by the light of an oil lamp. It has nothing to do with waste or anger."], ["General Awareness", "The Permanent Settlement of land revenue in Bengal (1793) was introduced by which Governor-General?", ["Warren Hastings", "Lord Dalhousie", "Lord Cornwallis", "Lord Wellesley"], 2, "Lord Cornwallis introduced the Permanent Settlement in 1793, fixing revenue permanently with zamindars. Wellesley is linked to the Subsidiary Alliance and Dalhousie to the Doctrine of Lapse."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "A's salary is 25% more than B's salary. By what percentage is B's salary less than A's?", ["22.5%", "20%", "15%", "25%"], 1, "If B = 100, then A = 125. B is less than A by 25, and 25/125 × 100 = 20%. The base changes to A's salary, which is why the answer is not 25%."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "A boat goes 18 km/h downstream and 12 km/h upstream. What is the speed of the stream?", ["15 km/h", "5 km/h", "6 km/h", "3 km/h"], 3, "Stream speed = (downstream − upstream)/2 = (18 − 12)/2 = 3 km/h. The value 15 km/h is the speed of the boat in still water."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "Select the number that completes the analogy.\n11 : 120 :: 13 : ?", ["168", "169", "156", "170"], 0, "Each first term is squared and then 1 is subtracted: 11² − 1 = 120. Applying the same rule, 13² − 1 = 169 − 1 = 168. The option 169 forgets the subtraction step."], ["General Awareness", "The hormone insulin is secreted by which organ of the human body?", ["Adrenal gland", "Pancreas", "Thyroid gland", "Liver"], 1, "Insulin is produced by the beta cells of the islets of Langerhans in the pancreas and lowers blood glucose. The liver stores glucose as glycogen but does not secrete insulin."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "What is the compound interest on ₹8,000 for 3 years at 10% per annum, compounded annually?", ["₹2,400", "₹2,840", "₹2,600", "₹2,648"], 3, "Amount = 8000 × (1.1)³ = 8000 × 1.331 = ₹10,648. CI = 10,648 − 8,000 = ₹2,648. ₹2,400 is the simple interest for the same period."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "If 3 # 4 = 25 and 5 # 12 = 169, then what is 6 # 8?", ["100", "196", "48", "14"], 0, "The rule is a # b = a² + b²: 9 + 16 = 25 and 25 + 144 = 169. So 6 # 8 = 36 + 64 = 100. The option 196 is (6 + 8)², a common slip."], ["General Awareness", "Who is credited with founding the Indian National Congress in 1885?", ["Dadabhai Naoroji", "W. C. Bonnerjee", "Surendranath Banerjee", "A. O. Hume"], 3, "Allan Octavian Hume, a retired British civil servant, took the initiative to found the Congress in 1885. W. C. Bonnerjee presided over its first session in Bombay, which makes him a tempting wrong choice."], ["General Awareness", "Black soil (regur) of the Deccan plateau is best suited for growing which crop?", ["Tea", "Rubber", "Cotton", "Jute"], 2, "Black soil retains moisture well and is rich in lime and magnesium, making it ideal for cotton, hence the name 'black cotton soil'. Tea needs acidic hill soils and jute grows in alluvial delta soils."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "If ROSE is coded as 6821, CHAIR as 73456 and PREACH as 961473, what is the code for SEARCH?", ["216473", "214673", "214763", "241673"], 1, "From the three codes: S = 2, E = 1, A = 4, R = 6, C = 7 and H = 3. Writing them in the order S-E-A-R-C-H gives 214673."], ["English Comprehension", "Select the correct indirect form of: She said to me, \"Please help me.\"", ["She told to me that please help her.", "She requested me to help her.", "She requested me that I help me.", "She said me to please help her."], 1, "A polite request with 'please' is reported with 'requested', and the imperative becomes a to-infinitive. The pronoun 'me' changes to 'her' to refer back to the speaker."], ["English Comprehension", "Read the passage and answer the question.\nRainwater harvesting is an old practice that has found new relevance in Indian cities. As groundwater levels fall, many housing societies now collect rooftop runoff and channel it into recharge pits instead of letting it flow into drains. The method is inexpensive and needs little maintenance, yet its benefits depend on cleaning the filters regularly before every monsoon.\nAccording to the passage, what do the benefits of rainwater harvesting depend on?", ["The number of drains available in the city", "Regular cleaning of filters before the monsoon", "The total cost of building large recharge pits", "Housing societies recruiting full-time staff"], 1, "The last sentence says the benefits 'depend on cleaning the filters regularly before every monsoon'. The passage calls the method inexpensive and low-maintenance, so cost and staffing are not the limiting factors."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "A trader sells two articles for ₹1,200 each. He gains 20% on one and loses 20% on the other. What is his overall result?", ["Loss of 4%", "No profit, no loss", "Loss of 2%", "Gain of 4%"], 0, "Cost prices are 1200/1.2 = ₹1,000 and 1200/0.8 = ₹1,500, total ₹2,500. Total selling price is ₹2,400, so loss = 100/2500 × 100 = 4%. Equal gain and loss percentages on equal SP always give a loss."], ["General Awareness", "What is the minimum age required to become a member of the Rajya Sabha?", ["25 years", "21 years", "30 years", "35 years"], 2, "Article 84 sets the minimum age at 30 years for the Rajya Sabha and 25 years for the Lok Sabha. 35 years is the minimum age for the President and Vice-President."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "₹7,800 is divided among A, B and C in the ratio 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/4. What is B's share?", ["₹2,400", "₹2,600", "₹3,600", "₹1,800"], 0, "Multiplying by the LCM 12, the ratio becomes 6 : 4 : 3, totalling 13 parts. One part = 7800/13 = ₹600, so B gets 4 × 600 = ₹2,400. ₹3,600 is A's share."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "Five friends A, B, C, D and E sit in a row facing North. C sits exactly in the middle and A sits to the immediate right of C. B sits at one of the extreme ends, and D does not sit next to C. Who sits to the immediate left of C?", ["B", "E", "D", "A"], 1, "C is 3rd and A is 4th from the left. B and D must take the two ends (D cannot be 2nd, as that is next to C), so the only seat left beside C, the 2nd one, goes to E."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "A man goes from his house to the office at 40 km/h and returns along the same route at 60 km/h. What is his average speed for the whole journey?", ["48 km/h", "45 km/h", "52 km/h", "50 km/h"], 0, "For equal distances, average speed = 2xy/(x + y) = 2 × 40 × 60 / 100 = 48 km/h. The simple average 50 km/h is wrong because more time is spent at the slower speed."], ["English Comprehension", "Fill in the blank with the most appropriate word.\nHardly had I reached the station ______ the train left.", ["when", "then", "but", "than"], 0, "'Hardly' and 'scarcely' are followed by 'when' (or 'before'). 'Than' is used with 'no sooner', which is the usual source of confusion."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "On which day of the week did 15 August 1947 fall?", ["Friday", "Sunday", "Saturday", "Thursday"], 0, "1600 years give 0 odd days, 300 years give 1 and 46 years give 4, so 1946 years give 5. 1 January–15 August 1947 has 227 days = 3 odd days. Total 8 ≡ 1 odd day, so the date fell on a Friday."], ["General Awareness", "Which Schedule of the Constitution of India lists the officially recognised languages?", ["Ninth Schedule", "Tenth Schedule", "Seventh Schedule", "Eighth Schedule"], 3, "The Eighth Schedule lists the languages recognised by the Constitution. The Seventh Schedule contains the Union, State and Concurrent Lists, and the Tenth deals with anti-defection."], ["General Awareness", "Which element has the highest electronegativity on the Pauling scale?", ["Chlorine", "Fluorine", "Nitrogen", "Oxygen"], 1, "Fluorine, with a value of about 4.0, is the most electronegative element. Oxygen (about 3.4) is second; chlorine has a higher electron affinity than fluorine but lower electronegativity, which often confuses students."], ["English Comprehension", "Select the one word for: 'A person who is unable to pay his or her debts'.", ["Indolent", "Inveterate", "Insolent", "Insolvent"], 3, "'Insolvent' describes a person or firm unable to pay debts. 'Insolent' means rude, 'indolent' means lazy and 'inveterate' means habitual; they look similar but differ in meaning."], ["General Awareness", "The Buland Darwaza at Fatehpur Sikri was built by which Mughal ruler?", ["Shah Jahan", "Humayun", "Aurangzeb", "Akbar"], 3, "Akbar built the Buland Darwaza around 1575–76 to commemorate his Gujarat campaign. Fatehpur Sikri itself was Akbar's capital; Shah Jahan is associated with the Taj Mahal and Red Fort."], ["English Comprehension", "Fill in the blank with the most appropriate word.\nThe thief was caught ______ the act of breaking the lock.", ["on", "by", "in", "at"], 2, "The fixed expression is 'caught in the act', meaning caught while doing something wrong. The other prepositions do not form this idiom."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "The average of five numbers is 24. When one number is removed, the average of the remaining numbers becomes 21. What is the number removed?", ["33", "45", "3", "36"], 3, "Sum of five numbers = 5 × 24 = 120; sum of remaining four = 4 × 21 = 84. The removed number = 120 − 84 = 36."], ["English Comprehension", "Choose the word closest in meaning to the word in capitals.\nThe minister gave a CANDID reply when reporters asked about the delay.", ["Cautious", "Rigid", "Frank", "Secretive"], 2, "'Candid' means honest and straightforward in speech, which matches 'frank'. 'Secretive' is nearly its opposite, while 'cautious' and 'rigid' describe unrelated qualities."], ["General Awareness", "Which is the highest peak in South India?", ["Dhupgarh", "Mahendragiri", "Anamudi", "Doddabetta"], 2, "Anamudi (about 2,695 m) in the Anaimalai Hills of Kerala is the highest peak south of the Himalayas. Doddabetta is the highest peak of the Nilgiris, and Dhupgarh is in the Satpura range."], ["English Comprehension", "Select the most appropriate improvement for the underlined part.\nThe number of students in the class 'are increasing' every year.", ["is increasing", "were increasing", "are increased", "have been increasing"], 0, "The subject is 'the number', which is singular, so the verb must be singular: 'is increasing'. 'A number of students' would take a plural verb, but 'the number of' does not."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "What is the LCM of 12, 18 and 30?", ["120", "180", "360", "90"], 1, "12 = 2²×3, 18 = 2×3² and 30 = 2×3×5. Taking the highest power of each prime: 2² × 3² × 5 = 180. 360 is a common multiple but not the least one."], ["General Awareness", "The Right to Education for children aged 6 to 14 years (Article 21A) was inserted into the Constitution by which amendment?", ["73rd Amendment Act, 1992", "86th Amendment Act, 2002", "42nd Amendment Act, 1976", "44th Amendment Act, 1978"], 1, "The 86th Amendment Act, 2002 inserted Article 21A, making free and compulsory education a Fundamental Right for children aged 6–14. It also added a related Fundamental Duty for parents and guardians."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "Pipe A can fill a tank in 10 hours and pipe B can empty the full tank in 15 hours. If both are opened together in an empty tank, in how many hours will it be filled?", ["25 hours", "12 hours", "6 hours", "30 hours"], 3, "Net filling per hour = 1/10 − 1/15 = 1/30 of the tank, so it fills in 30 hours. 6 hours would be the answer only if both pipes were filling."], ["General Awareness", "Which group of chemicals is chiefly responsible for depletion of the stratospheric ozone layer?", ["Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs)", "Nitrogen and argon", "Carbon dioxide and methane", "Sulphur dioxide and ammonia"], 0, "CFCs release chlorine atoms in the stratosphere that break down ozone molecules. Carbon dioxide and methane are greenhouse gases linked to global warming, not the main cause of ozone depletion."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "Select the number that does NOT belong to the group.\n27, 64, 100, 125", ["27", "100", "125", "64"], 1, "27, 64 and 125 are perfect cubes (3³, 4³ and 5³). 100 is a perfect square (10²) but not a perfect cube, so it is the odd one out."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "If 'A + B' means A is the mother of B and 'A × B' means A is the brother of B, then what does 'P × Q + R' mean about P with respect to R?", ["P is the father of R", "P is the paternal uncle of R", "P is the maternal uncle of R", "P is the brother of R"], 2, "P × Q means P is Q's brother, and Q + R means Q is R's mother. The brother of one's mother is one's maternal uncle, so P is R's maternal uncle."], ["English Comprehension", "Select the correct passive form of: Who wrote this letter?", ["By whom has this letter been written?", "Who was written this letter by?", "By whom this letter was written?", "By whom was this letter written?"], 3, "An interrogative with 'who' becomes 'by whom' in the passive, keeping question word order: By whom + was + object + past participle. The present perfect option changes the tense."], ["English Comprehension", "Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.\nNeither the manager nor his assistants / was present / at the meeting / held yesterday.", ["Neither the manager nor his assistants", "held yesterday", "at the meeting", "was present"], 3, "With 'neither…nor', the verb agrees with the nearer subject. Here the nearer subject 'assistants' is plural, so 'was present' should be 'were present'."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "In a certain code language, CHAIR is written as AFYGP. How will SOFA be written in that language?", ["RMDY", "UQHC", "QMDY", "QMDZ"], 2, "Every letter is moved two places back in the alphabet: C→A, H→F, A→Y, I→G, R→P. So S→Q, O→M, F→D and A→Y, giving QMDY. UQHC wrongly shifts letters forward."], ["English Comprehension", "Choose the word opposite in meaning to the word in capitals.\nThe fame of most viral videos is EPHEMERAL.", ["Permanent", "Transient", "Fleeting", "Momentary"], 0, "'Ephemeral' means lasting a very short time. 'Fleeting', 'transient' and 'momentary' are all synonyms, so the only antonym is 'permanent'."], ["General Awareness", "Fiscal deficit of the government is best defined as:", ["Fiscal deficit minus interest payments on past debt", "Revenue expenditure minus revenue receipts", "Total expenditure minus total receipts excluding borrowings", "Total expenditure minus revenue receipts and all borrowings"], 2, "Fiscal deficit = total expenditure − (revenue receipts + non-debt capital receipts), i.e. it equals the government's borrowing requirement. Revenue expenditure minus revenue receipts is the revenue deficit; deficit minus interest is primary deficit."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "What is the angle between the hour hand and the minute hand of a clock at 4:20?", ["5°", "0°", "20°", "10°"], 3, "Angle = |30H − 5.5M| = |30 × 4 − 5.5 × 20| = |120 − 110| = 10°. The hour hand moves 10° beyond the 4 in 20 minutes, which is why the hands do not overlap."], ["General Intelligence & Reasoning", "A person is facing North. He turns 90° clockwise, then 135° anticlockwise, and then 180° clockwise. Which direction is he facing now?", ["South-East", "North-East", "North-West", "South-West"], 0, "Measuring clockwise from North: 0° + 90° = 90° (East), 90° − 135° = −45° (North-West), then −45° + 180° = 135°, which is South-East. North-West is the position before the last turn."], ["Quantitative Aptitude", "If a + b = 10 and ab = 21, what is the value of a² + b²?", ["100", "79", "58", "42"], 2, "a² + b² = (a + b)² − 2ab = 100 − 42 = 58. Check: a = 7 and b = 3 satisfy both conditions, and 49 + 9 = 58."], ["General Awareness", "Which mountain pass connects Srinagar with Leh?", ["Zoji La", "Nathu La", "Bomdi La", "Shipki La"], 0, "Zoji La links the Kashmir valley with Ladakh on the Srinagar–Leh route. Nathu La is in Sikkim, Shipki La in Himachal Pradesh and Bomdi La in Arunachal Pradesh."]]};
